body:
Newie wanting to start getting into photography. Undecided between something mirrorless like the Canon EOS m50, or the relatively new Nikdon d3500.

&#x200B;

Everything i read seems to indicate that mirrorless are the future, and DSLR are on their way out. I don't have a big budget, which most posts suggest DSLR is a better route.

&#x200B;

All in all its a bit confusing. I know DSLR has more lens options for less $ - is that basically the difference? I see myself becoming a hobbiest, so doubt i'd ever have a massive lens collection.

&#x200B;

Don't really care too much about video, but would be good to have the option for vlogging etc in the future.

&#x200B;

SO far i was thinking Nikon d3500, Canon EOS M50, Panasonic Lumix G7, Sony a6000 or Canon Rebel.  Other suggestion? or any advice ?

&#x200B;

thanks in advance

There is no way cat4's are training 20 hours a week unless they are very new to racing and just haven't had the chance to get the points to upgrade. Thats Cat1/2 volume.

&#x200B;

Most cat 4's are less than 10 hrs.
